# L §8.4 Load refuses what load sees, L §2.5 (tally 2.1.7 R5, issue #144; #106): a literal key at a literal
# stepped range is load's to refuse wherever it is written, a def no ask reads included, whatever the asks.
# 2.1.6's refcore checked only rows, at the first ask answered, and answered q (0).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input r[d in 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 days]: int

def w: int = r[2026-01-09]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  r[*] = 0 "s"

ask q: r[2026-01-15]
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY 2026-01-09 is not a value of 2026-01-01 .. 2026-12-31 step 7 day ...
